# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# BMW 7 Series G70 four-door saloon, 2022-.
#
# The seventh 7-series: the CLAR-platform car revealed in April 2022, sold in
# Britain from December 2022 as the i7, with the 750e and M760e from spring
# 2023. There is no short-wheelbase G70: every car is 5.391 m on a 3.215 m
# wheelbase. The split headlamps and the tall kidney grille are the defining
# features and both are modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_7_Series_(G70)
#
# Dimensions 5.391 x 1.950 x 1.544 m, wheelbase 3.215 m, from the BMW G70
# technical data table (2022 price-list PDF) and the UK launch reports. Mirrors
# take the modelled width to 2.220 m.
#
# Colours: the UK launch palette, BMW names:
#   Alpine White (solid)    300
#   Black Sapphire meta.    475
#   Brooklyn Grey meta.     C4P
#   Oxide Grey metallic     C4A
# The UK brochure and the paint-code index support availability; the colours
# are recorded as launch-palette offerings rather than as measured popularity,
# which does not exist for a car this recent. Isle of Man Green and the
# two-tone Individual finishes are left out.
# Weights black 3, grey 3, silver 2, white 2, total 10, provisional pending the
# central rebase.
#
# Speed 250 km/h, the limiter on the 750e and M760e; the i7 is quoted at
# 240 km/h but the same body is modelled once. Comfort 180/600, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 180, the highest private-car value in the pakset and a step above
# the G11's 175/593. Classes 3,4.
#
# Dates are road presence: December 2022 intro, retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026)
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-g70.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-g70.dae (78 objects). References:
# citycars/references/bmw-g70/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons; the cars
# photographed are Korean-market Design Pure Excellence cars, and the UK-only
# powertrain badging and charging flap are deliberately not modelled).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the nose and
# tail are more angular than the photographs, the front overhang reads slightly
# long against the profile photograph, and the two-level headlamp treatment is
# simplified. At 128 px the tall grille, the split lamps and the long
# wheelbase read as the G70.

obj=citycar
